From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:47:20 +0200
Subject: nv30: a fragment program that closes an IF or a loop at its end is
 ended by the appended NOP and END

The translator set END on the last instruction it emitted and appended a NOP and
END for branches to the end of the program. When the program's last TGSI
instruction closes an IF or a loop, that last instruction is inside it: its
ELSE and ENDIF targets and the loop's end are the appended slot, past the first
END. Whether the GPU stops at the first END it executes or loads the program up
to it, the encoding is wrong or at least ambiguous (a loop ending a program ran
once), and the RSX driver's program check refuses a branch target past the
program's first END.

END is now left off the last instruction in that case, and only the appended NOP
carries it. Programs that close their structures before the last instruction
are unchanged.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nvfx_fragprog.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nvfx_fragprog.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nvfx_fragprog.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nvfx_fragprog.c
@@ -1119,6 +1119,7 @@ _nvfx_fragprog_translate(uint16_t oclass, struct nv30_fragprog *fp)
 
    tgsi_parse_init(&parse, fp->pipe.tokens);
    insns = UTIL_DYNARRAY_INIT;
+   enum tgsi_opcode last_op = TGSI_OPCODE_END;   /* the last one before END */
 
    while (!tgsi_parse_end_of_tokens(&parse)) {
       tgsi_parse_token(&parse);
@@ -1130,6 +1131,8 @@ _nvfx_fragprog_translate(uint16_t oclass, struct nv30_fragprog *fp)
 
          util_dynarray_append(&insns, fp->insn_len);
          finst = &parse.FullToken.FullInstruction;
+         if (finst->Instruction.Opcode != TGSI_OPCODE_END)
+            last_op = finst->Instruction.Opcode;
          if (!nvfx_fragprog_parse_instruction(fpc, finst))
             goto out_err;
       }
@@ -1152,8 +1155,11 @@ _nvfx_fragprog_translate(uint16_t oclass, struct nv30_fragprog *fp)
    else
       fp->fp_control |= fpc->num_regs << NV40_3D_FP_CONTROL_TEMP_COUNT__SHIFT;
 
-   /* Terminate final instruction */
-   if(fp->insn)
+   /* Terminate final instruction. Not when the program closes an IF or a loop at its end: the
+    * last instruction is then inside it, the structure ends on the NOP + END appended below, and
+    * an END before that target ends the program early (after one iteration of a loop) or leaves
+    * the branch target past the program's end, which the RSX driver's checker refuses. */
+   if(fp->insn && last_op != TGSI_OPCODE_ENDIF && last_op != TGSI_OPCODE_ENDLOOP)
       fp->insn[fpc->inst_offset] |= 0x00000001;
 
    /* Append NOP + END instruction for branches to the end of the program */
